('128.35.c.9.A',3,'A classic novel written long ago and still read today is an example of:','["a menu", "a bus pass", "world literature across periods", "a brochure"]'::jsonb,2,'Literature spans time.','original'),
('128.35.c.9.B',4,'In poetry, ''rain'' and ''train'' at line endings form an:','["free verse", "slant rhyme", "internal rhyme", "end rhyme"]'::jsonb,3,'End rhymes occur at line ends.','original'),
('128.35.c.9.B',4,'A rhyme inside a single line is an:','["internal rhyme", "title rhyme", "end rhyme", "stanza break"]'::jsonb,0,'Internal rhyme occurs within a line.','original'),
('128.35.c.9.C',4,'In a play, the audience knows a secret the characters do not. This is:','["a soliloquy", "dramatic irony", "an aside", "a stage direction"]'::jsonb,1,'Dramatic irony depends on audience knowledge.','original'),
('128.35.c.9.C',4,'Stage directions in a script tell actors and directors:','["the price", "the bibliography", "how to move and speak", "the index"]'::jsonb,2,'Stage directions guide performance.','original'),
('128.35.c.9.D.i',3,'An essay conclusion should:','["stop mid-idea", "list sources", "introduce a new topic", "restate the thesis and give a final thought"]'::jsonb,3,'Conclusions close the argument.','original'),
('128.35.c.9.D.i',3,'Pertinent examples in an essay are:','["examples that clearly relate to the thesis", "any interesting story", "facts from another topic", "jokes only"]'::jsonb,0,'Pertinent means relevant.','original'),
('128.35.c.9.D.ii',3,'A caption under a photograph in an article explains:','["who printed the page", "what the picture shows", "the author''s age", "the table of contents"]'::jsonb,1,'Captions describe images.','original'),
